.TH std::any::~any 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::any::~any \- std::any::~any

.SH Synopsis
~any();  \fI(since C++17)\fP

Destroys the contained object, if any, as if by a call to reset().

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <any>
#include <cstdio>

struct X
{
    X() { std::puts("X::X()"); }
    X(const X&) { std::puts("X::X(const X&)"); }
    ~X() { std::puts("X::~X()"); }
};

int main()
{
    std::any a{X{}};
    std::puts("Leaving main()...");
}

.SH Output:

X::X()
X::X(const X&)
X::~X()
Leaving main()...
X::~X()

.SH See also

reset destroys contained object
      \fI(public member function)\fP
